---
globs: members/**/*.spec.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

## Testing Principles

- test user behavior, not implementation details
- follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern

## Setup Function

- create a `setup()` function with an options parameter to control the "Arrange" phase
- provide sensible defaults in the options parameter so tests don't need to pass options when using default behavior
- setup should ONLY handle "Arrange" - never include user actions (Act) in setup
- return mocked services and other test utilities from setup

## User Events

- `const user = userEvent.setup()` should be created inside the setup function and returned
- use `user` variable name consistently
- destructure `user` from setup in each test

## Routing

- avoid testing routing in component tests - this is integration testing, not unit testing
- if a component navigates, that's an implementation detail - don't test it
- test user behavior and UI state changes, not navigation calls
- routing should be tested in integration/e2e tests, not component specs

## Mock Components

- use minimal mock components with clear, testable content
- follow same component patterns as real components (ChangeDetection.OnPush, etc.)
